# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# T4 benchmark .gitignore
#
# NOTE: results/ and analysis/figures/ are intentionally NOT ignored. They are
# the reproducible artifacts (raw pilot records, measured metrics, and paper
# figures) and are committed so reviewers can inspect them without re-running
# the harness. `make reproduce-small` regenerates the data artifacts
# byte-for-byte and the figure PNGs pixel-for-pixel (PNG container bytes differ
# across platforms) — see README "Reproducibility and determinism".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Model-evaluation output (generation/runner). Unlike the pilot artifacts above,
# these are stochastic model outputs rather than deterministic harness output:
# they do not reproduce byte-for-byte, they grow without bound across runs, and
# committing a smoke-test run would let it masquerade as a measured result.
# Archive a real run deliberately (`git add -f`) if you want it in the record.
/results/raw/
/results/model_results.json

# Go build output
/bin/
*.test
*.out
*.exe
*.exe~
*.o
*.a
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Go workspace / vendor (this repo uses no external deps)
/vendor/
go.work
go.work.sum

# Python artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
.env/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Bundled results archive (build artifact, regenerate with `make model-figures` + zip)
/t4_results_bundle.zip
